WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:17.710
Nello held the leather bag in his hand.

2
00:00:17.711 --> 00:00:21.878
He had never seen so much money before.

3
00:00:21.879 --> 00:00:27.551
He put the bag in his shirt and patted Patrasche on the head.

4
00:00:27.552 --> 00:00:30.996
Nello walked straight toward the mill.

5
00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.763
He knocked on the front door.

6
00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:37.127
The miller's wife opened the door.

7
00:00:37.128 --> 00:00:39.745
Alois stood behind her.

8
00:00:39.746 --> 00:00:42.564
Both looked very upset.

9
00:00:42.565 --> 00:00:45.554
"What is it, Nello?" Alois asked.

10
00:00:45.555 --> 00:00:49.322
"Go before my father sees you!"

11
00:00:49.323 --> 00:00:55.005
"Master Cogez is in a terrible mood tonight," the miller's wife said.

12
00:00:55.006 --> 00:00:59.417
"He dropped some money and, in this snow, he will never find it.

13
00:00:59.418 --> 00:01:04.046
It was all our savings," she sobbed.

14
00:01:04.047 --> 00:01:09.709
Nello stepped inside and gave the leather bag to the miller's wife.

15
00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:13.053
He called Patrasche into the house.

16
00:01:13.054 --> 00:01:18.590
"Patrasche found the money in the snow," Nello said.

17
00:01:18.591 --> 00:01:23.377
"Tell Master Cogez to please look after Patrasche.

18
00:01:23.378 --> 00:01:27.632
I can't take care of him anymore."

19
00:01:27.633 --> 00:01:31.837
Nello bent down to kiss Patrasche good-bye.

20
00:01:31.838 --> 00:01:37.152
Then he quickly closed the door and disappeared into the night.

21
00:01:37.153 --> 00:01:41.413
The miller's wife and daughter were speechless.

22
00:01:41.414 --> 00:01:45.006
Patrasche went to the door and whined.

23
00:01:45.007 --> 00:01:50.013
He wanted to follow Nello, but the door was closed.

24
00:01:50.014 --> 00:01:54.267
Alois and her mother tried to comfort Patrasche.

25
00:01:54.268 --> 00:01:57.725
They brought him milk and a big bone.

26
00:01:57.726 --> 00:02:04.541
They gave him a blanket to lie on near the warm fire. Nothing worked.

27
00:02:04.542 --> 00:02:10.264
Patrasche sat stubbornly by the door and would not move.

28
00:02:10.265 --> 00:02:13.800
At six o'clock the miller came home.

29
00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:18.017
He looked very tired and his face was sad.

30
00:02:18.018 --> 00:02:22.528
"The money is lost forever," he said.

31
00:02:22.529 --> 00:02:27.368
"I took a lantern and looked everywhere, but it's gone.

32
00:02:27.369 --> 00:02:31.874
Some of that money was for Alois' future.

33
00:02:31.875 --> 00:02:35.362
I'm so sorry, Alois."

34
00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:40.299
His wife put the money into his hands and told him the story.

35
00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:44.203
The miller walked to a chair by the fire.

36
00:02:44.204 --> 00:02:48.346
He sat down and covered his face, ashamed.

37
00:02:48.347 --> 00:02:52.202
"I have been cruel to the boy," he muttered.

38
00:02:52.203 --> 00:02:55.823
"I don't deserve his goodness."

39
00:02:55.824 --> 00:02:59.765
Little Alois crept close to her father.

40
00:02:59.766 --> 00:03:05.057
"Can Nello come here again, Father?" she whispered bravely.

41
00:03:05.058 --> 00:03:08.983
"Can he come and play tomorrow, like he used to?"

42
00:03:08.984 --> 00:03:12.418
The miller hugged his daughter tightly.

43
00:03:12.419 --> 00:03:16.333
His lips trembled with emotion.

44
00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:21.526
"Yes, of course Nello can play with you," the miller said.

45
00:03:21.527 --> 00:03:26.141
"He can come here on Christmas Day, and any day of the year.

46
00:03:26.142 --> 00:03:29.736
I have treated Nello very badly.

47
00:03:29.737 --> 00:03:32.374
I must make it up to him."

48
00:03:32.375 --> 00:03:36.345
Little Alois kissed her father with joy.

49
00:03:36.346 --> 00:03:40.355
She ran to where Patrasche sat by the door.

50
00:03:40.356 --> 00:03:45.664
Patrasche was still waiting and hoping that Nello would return.

51
00:03:45.665 --> 00:03:49.637
They had never spent a night apart.

52
00:03:49.638 --> 00:03:53.140
"And tonight may I give Patrasche lots of food?"

53
00:03:53.141 --> 00:03:56.561
she asked, giving the dog a hug.

54
00:03:56.562 --> 00:03:59.312
Her father looked at her.

55
00:03:59.313 --> 00:04:02.856
The stubbornness had washed from his face.

56
00:04:02.857 --> 00:04:08.664
"Yes, yes. Let the dog have the best food," he said.

57
00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:14.797
The miller sat with his head in his hand and was quiet for a long time.

58
00:04:14.798 --> 00:04:19.013
He thought about his actions over and over.

59
00:04:19.014 --> 00:04:23.744
Nello was only fifteen years old and had nothing.

60
00:04:23.745 --> 00:04:33.960
"Even so," the miller thought, "he is a better man than me."
